// SIC bounds (sic.md §"Bounds"): a `new` array moved inside `unsafe { }` is
// checked against its allocation (the reassignment was not seen, and the size
// was read from the wrong place). `a[3]` is element 9 of 8. Exit 134 (abort).
int main() {
    int *a = new int[8];
    unsafe { a = a + 6; }
    a[3] = 1;
    return 0;
}
